# Conventions

## Directory surface

A directory's public surface is its `mod.ts`. Import that file from outside
the directory. Do not reach into a sibling module (`routing/pipeline.ts`,
`shared/shared_types.ts`). Same-directory imports are fine.

## Route modules

A `*_route.ts(x)` module exports route handlers and nothing else, and only
the route table imports from it. Shared values live in a module that is not
a route.

Application code never calls a handler. The router is what invokes one: a
direct call skips the target's middleware and error boundary, applies its
cache policy to the caller's response, and leaves it reading the caller's
`ctx`. Share markup as a component, including between two methods of one
route, and use `<RouteFragment src>` to include another route's rendered
output.

## Discriminants

A closed set of cases is a `const enum`. Comparisons use the enum member, not
a string literal. Use a plain `enum` only when a const enum cannot (it must
exist at runtime as an object).

## Object types

An object shape is an `interface`. `type` is for unions, aliases, mapped
types, and everything that is not a single object shape.

## Type assertions

Do not assert (`as`) to silence the checker. An assertion is allowed when
the types cannot express the fact, and only at the use that needs it, with
a note saying why. Prefer restructuring so the assertion is unnecessary.

## Helpers

Do not extract a function that is a short, obvious check or a few
straightforward lines used once. Inline it until extraction earns its keep.
Extract when the same non-trivial shape is repeated, or when the body is long
or not obvious (`withoutContent`). A one-line env read used once stays at the
call site.

## Client JS

Client TypeScript attaches only via `client.module` / `client.element` at
module scope. The factory throws after compile. App files are `*_client.ts`
and sit beside the module that registers them. The factory returns a
PascalCase component; `client.element` takes the custom element tag
(kebab-case). Compiled files are served at `/_dashi/client/` by a reserved
table route. Public URLs are flat `/_dashi/client/<name>-<hash>.js`.
Relative imports in compiled files are rewritten to the matching
bundler path. The import map is bundler path → flat hashed URL.
Documents get one `<script type="importmap">` for that graph;
a module script is added only when a host rendered. A lazy fragment
`import()`s its `Link` modulepreloads before swap.
`DASHI_MINIFY_CLIENT=1` minifies the bundle; `deno task dev` sets it to `0`.
`staticFile` is app-mounted disk files. `/_dashi/*` is reserved.
